"Let $P$ be a finite poset. For a positive integer $n$, let $\\operatorname{La}(n,P)$ be the maximum size of a $P$-free family of subsets of $[n]$. For positive integers $n$ and $x<n$, write $\\binom{[n]}{x}$ for the family of $x$-element subsets of $[n]$. Define $e(P)$ to be the largest integer $\\ell$ such that, for all $j$ and $n$, the family\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i=1}^{\\ell}\\binom{[n]}{i+j}\n$$\n\nis $P$-free.\n\n**The asymptotic extremal-size conjecture.** For every poset $P$,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{La}(n,P)=e(P)\\binom{n}{\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor}(1+o(1)).\n$$\n\nThis conjecture generalizes Sperner's theorem. It is unresolved for the two-dimensional Boolean lattice, but has been disproved for the $d$-dimensional Boolean lattice when $d\\geq 4$."